PIN_NOTES={
 'kent-iron-furnace':WKA+' It is the same spot an address lookup gives for the museum, 31 Kent-Cornwall Road. On the Esri satellite it falls in the museum clearing beside a small building, about 100 m from the river; the furnace stack itself was not picked out, so walk down the hill toward the river from there.',
 'mine-hill-roxbury':WKA+' OpenStreetMap maps the site ("Mine Hill National Historic Landmark") within 50 m. On the Esri satellite (leaves off) the ring falls in woods with a dark square structure about 30 m to the north-west, which may be a furnace stack; not confirmed.',
 'sharon-valley-lime-kiln':OSMA+' ("Lime Kiln", Sharon Station Road). On the New York leaf-off aerial the ring falls on a small dark structure at the edge of the road, beside the creek, which fits the kiln.',
 'falls-village-canal':'Pin was placed by eye in the strip between Water Street and the railroad that the National Register boundary describes, opposite the power house. The stone walls were not picked out under the trees on the Esri satellite: treat it as the vicinity.',
 'canaan-union-depot':WKA+' On the Esri satellite the ring falls on the station building in the angle of the two rail lines.',
 'terryville-waterwheel':OSMA+' ("Terryville Waterwheel", Main Street). On the Esri satellite the ring falls on a small roofed structure on the north side of Main Street.',
 'northfield-knife-company':OSMA+' ("Knife Shop Dam"). The federal protected-areas map puts a point 60 m south of it in Humaston Brook State Park. The ruins are below the dam, south of Knife Shop Road, under trees on the Esri satellite; they were not picked out.',
 'borden-condensed-milk':'The Wikipedia coordinate for the park falls in the middle of Burr Pond. The pin was moved to an address lookup of the park\'s address, 384 Burr Mountain Road; on the Esri satellite that is the road through woods north-east of the pond, not a building. The factory foundations were not located; treat the pin as the vicinity and look for the bronze tablet.',
 'lovers-leap-ruins':OSMA+' for the park ("Lovers Leap State Park"). The ruins are in the north-west part of the park near the water; the Esri satellite shows bare woods above the river, and no ruin was picked out.',
 'cunningham-tower':OSMA+' ("Cunningham Tower", man_made=tower). On the Esri satellite the ring falls on a round dark structure in a small clearing.',
 'camp-columbia':WKA+' On the Esri satellite (leaves on) it falls on a clearing where paths meet, on the old campus; the tower was not picked out.',
 'leatherman-cave-watertown':OSMA+' ("Rock House", a cave entrance in Watertown), which is the shelter at Crane\'s Lookout. On the Esri satellite (leaves on) a pale patch of rock shows in the ring. The other shelters people call the real cave were not pinned.',
 'bear-mountain-monument':OSMA+' ("Bear Mountain", a viewpoint on the Appalachian Trail); the Wikipedia coordinate is within 30 m. On the Esri satellite a pale square stone structure sits just inside the ring.',
 'steep-rock-tunnel':'Pin is the middle of the trail mapped in OpenStreetMap as a tunnel (way 410252977, 85 m long), read from the copy Esri hosts. On the Esri satellite it is dense conifers on the ridge above the Shepaug; the tunnel cannot be seen from above.',
 'holiday-house-steep-rock':OSMA+' ("Holiday House ruins", Kirby Brook Road). On the Esri satellite (leaves off) it is bare woods; no foundation was picked out, so the precision was lowered.',
}
